  "implementationNotes": [
    "Year2 means the entire current two-year status period, never just its second year. Compare year1 OR year2; freeze the first-period total after its deadline.",
    "Use the dates and totals displayed by the Miles&Smiles account when available. Store officialFirstPeriodEndDate explicitly; do not derive renewal dates from calendar-year boundaries. Initial promotion expiry and renewed-cycle expiry use different formulas.",
    "For an upgrade projection at a future flight date, recompute the rolling 12-month window at that future date so older entries fall out. Do not add planned miles to today's rolling total without aging it.",
    "Show current credited totals separately from planned forecasts. Cancelled records count zero; completed but uncredited flights do not count as already qualified.",
    "Do not downgrade a currently valid tier because its rolling 12-month total is lower today. The rolling counter answers upgrade eligibility only.",
    "Residence affects Elite renewal only in this data. Ask Turkey/abroad explicitly; nationality is a different field.",
    "Do not turn every paid flight into an eligible flight count. Record an explicit confirmed eligiblePaidFlights value, or label the result as an estimate.",
    "Do not add statusMiles and redeemableMiles together. Flights may credit both counters, status purchases credit only status, and card conversions debit eligible spendable miles.",
    "Store activityDate and creditedDate separately. The public sources do not settle every retroactive-credit and exact boundary-date case; prefer official account period totals there.",
    "Purchase and conversion eligibility can depend on account history; present rules and estimates without promising that THY will accept a transaction."
  ],
  "unresolvedBoundaries": [
    "The public page says preceding 12 months but does not specify inclusive/exclusive anniversary-day treatment. A day-based estimate may use (asOf minus 12 calendar months, asOf]; flag an activity exactly on that boundary.",
    "The public page defines first period as the first year from status start, without an explicit boundary-day example. A fallback can use [start, add_calendar_years(start, 1)); label it estimated and allow officialFirstPeriodEndDate override.",
    "Exact airline eligibility for Classic Plus flight counts is not enumerated on the public status page. Use confirmed account counts for certainty.",
    "Do not promise a particular downgrade tier after failed renewal without verifying the member's account and relevant rule."
  ],
